                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you've searched how to reset service trailer brakes, chances are you're dealing with a warning message that appeared at the worst possible time. The first instinct is often to find a quick reset and get back on the road. But while resetting the warning may seem like the fastest option, it doesn't always address the issue causing it in the first place. When it comes to trailer brake systems, the safest approach is identifying the cause of the warning instead of simply trying to clear it.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-what-means",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Does the Service Trailer Brake Warning Mean?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "what-means"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-means-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A service trailer brake warning is designed to alert drivers that something within the braking system may need attention. Depending on the trailer and braking setup, the issue could involve:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-what-means-2",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Electrical connection problems"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Wiring concerns"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Faulty sensors"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Brake controller issues"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Air brake system irregularities"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Wear within braking components"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Communication failures between the truck and trailer"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-means-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Because modern braking systems are increasingly complex, the same warning light can have multiple causes. This is why understanding how to reset the trailer brake system warnings should start with understanding why the warning appeared in the first place.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-reset-yourself",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Can You Reset the Service Trailer Brake System Yourself?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "reset-yourself"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-reset-yourself-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Technically, some vehicles may allow drivers to clear warning messages through dashboard controls or after disconnecting and reconnecting the trailer. However, that doesn't necessarily solve the problem. Think of it this way: if your smoke detector goes off because of a fire, removing the battery doesn't eliminate the fire. The same concept applies here.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-reset-yourself-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A reset may temporarily clear the message, but if there's an underlying issue affecting the braking system, the warning is likely to return. More importantly, continuing to operate equipment with unresolved brake concerns can increase safety risks and potentially lead to more extensive semi trailer repair needs later.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
